codex
The paper’s native task is more constrained than “find some planted paths”: every arc of a fixed multidigraph \(H\) must be replaced by a directed path of a prescribed length at least 4, all paths internally vertex-disjoint, with prescribed branch vertices. The main theorem is existential for sufficiently large dense oriented graphs, so I’m now checking whether its proof is algorithmic enough to make linkage search easy on the generated distribution—and whether a native generator can avoid leaking its planted linkage.
