/tmp/tmp.aqKRdKTQwi/final-Semi-Degree_Condition_for_Arbitrary_H-Linked.tex:894:Similarly, $|S^{l''}_{i}| > \theta |V_{l'}|/2 $. The $\varepsilon$-regularity of $(V_{l'}, V_{l''})$ implies that $|d(S^{l'}_{i}, S^{l''}_{i}) - d(V_{l'}, V_{l''})| < \varepsilon$. Hence, $d(S^{l'}_{i}, S^{l''}_{i}) \geq d - \varepsilon \geq 5d/6$. For any two vertex sets $U'\subseteq S^{l'}_{i}$ of order $\sqrt{\varepsilon}|S^{l'}_{i}| $ and $U''\subseteq S^{l''}_{i}$ of order $ \sqrt{\varepsilon}|S^{l''}_{i}|$, because $ \sqrt{\varepsilon}|S^{l'}_{i}|> \sqrt{\varepsilon}\theta |V_{l'}|/2 >\varepsilon |V_{l'}|,$ {we have that} $|d(U', U'') - d(V_{l'}, V_{l''})| < \varepsilon$. This implies that $|d(U', U'') - d(S^{l'}_{i}, S^{l''}_{i})| < 2\varepsilon<\sqrt{\varepsilon}$, then by definition, $(S^{l'}_{i}, S^{l''}_{i})$ is $\sqrt{\varepsilon}$-regular pair. In light of the construction of $R$, if $(V_{l'}, V_{l''})$ is $\varepsilon$-regular with density at as least $d$, then $(S^{l'}_{i}, S^{l''}_{i})$ is $\sqrt{\varepsilon}$-regular pair with density at least $5d/6$. This leads to the conclusion that $R_{i}$ is the reduced oriented graph of $\widetilde{S}_{i}$ corresponding to the partition $(S^0_{i},S^1_{i}, \ldots,S^M_{i})$, {with parameters \(\sqrt{\varepsilon}\) and \(5d/6\) in place of \(\varepsilon\) and $d$ respectively,} as desired.
