$$
\delta^0(\widehat{D}) \geq \tfrac{3n-4}{8} - (h + q\theta n) \stackrel{(\ref{para1})(\ref{para2})}> \tfrac{n}{3} + 6.
$$
 Apply Lemma~\ref{lemma3} with $ l:=|P_{q - i}| < \theta n \stackrel{(\ref{para1})}< |\widehat{D}|/10^{10}$ to get the path $P_{q - i}$ in $\widehat{D}=(D\setminus (W\cup B))\cup \{u_{q - i},v_{q - i}\}$. Therefore, we obtain all short subdivision paths. Update $W := \bigcup^{q}_{i = s + 1} P_{i}$, and then we have $|W|< q\theta n $.

For the construction of long paths, we first apply {Diregularity Lemma} and random partition to divide the remaining oriented graph into $s$ subgraphs, each with a specified order. Through pinch vertex operation, we transform the problem of constructing long subdivision paths into finding Hamilton cycles in these subgraphs. Finally, we complete the proof by using Lemma \ref{4.5}.

 Let $ D^* = D - (W \cup B) $, then
$
