The paper’s main result is existential for very dense oriented graphs; its proof constructs short paths directly, then reduces long paths to Hamilton cycles after random partitioning and vertex pinching. I’m now checking whether that witness-search route is algorithmic/cheap in the shipping regime and whether the proposed planted family would retain enough solution sparsity to satisfy H—dense graphs may otherwise make valid subdivisions far too abundant.
