$$\sum_{v\in D_1} d_{D\setminus B}^-(v)\leq \frac{|D_1|\cdot (|D_1-1|)}{2}+ a(M)n/150+ |D_1|\cdot |D_4|,$$
$$\sum_{v\in D_2} d_{D\setminus B}(v)\leq (|D_1|+|D_3|)\cdot |D_2| + 2a(M)n/150+|D_2|\cdot |D_4|,$$
$$\sum_{v\in D_3} d_{D\setminus B}^+(v)\leq \frac{|D_3|\cdot (|D_3-1|)}{2}+ a(M)n/150+ |D_3|\cdot |D_4|.$$


 By pigeonhole principle, there are three vertices $u\in D_1, v\in D_2, w\in D_3$ such that
$$d_{D\setminus B}^-(u)\leq \frac{|D_1|-1}{2}+|D_4|+\frac{a(M)n}{150 |D_1|}<\frac{|D_1|-1}{2}+|D_4|+\frac{a(M)}{30},$$
$$d_{D\setminus B}(v)<|D_1|+|D_3|+|D_4|+ \frac{a(M)}{15},\ \text{ and } d_{D\setminus B}^+(w)<\frac{|D_3|-1}{2} + |D_4| + \frac{a(M)}{30}.$$
Together $|D_2| - |D_4|-b=r>a(M)$ with $|D_1|+|D_2|+|D_3|+|D_4|= n-h$, it yields that
\begin{equation}\label{2}
\begin{aligned}
4\times \frac{3n+3h+3q-5}{8}-3h&\leq d_{D\setminus B}^-(u) + d_{D\setminus B}^+(w) + d_{D\setminus B}(v) \\
&<\frac{3}{2}(n-h-|D_2| + |D_4|)+ \frac{2a(M)}{15} -1.
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
 Thus (\ref{2}) gives that $0\leq 41(|D_2|-|D_4|)/30+2b/15<-(3q-3)/2.$ This is impossible.
