where $\eta _0$ as stated in Lemma \ref{4.3}. For brevity, we denote \(n_0^{(a)}\) as the constant \(n_0\) in Lemma \(a\) or Theorem \(a\). To ensure that the oriented graphs in Theorem \ref{main} is large enough so that the above conclusions can be utilized, we select \(n_0^{(1.1)}\) to satisfy
