Built a self-contained Track B generator based on the paper’s native one-loop \(H\)-subdivision problem. The [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.06675) provides no distributional hardness basis for Track A.

Key results:

- All local G1–G9 gates pass.
- Structured guesses: 0/200,000.
- Four attacks: each 0/8.
- Reference Camion algorithm: 8/8, as expected for Track B.
- Answer: 48 atoms, 135 characters.
- Compact route: 276 exact operations.
- Canonical-key tests: 80/80 invariant; 20/20 unrelated instances distinct.

Files:

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2407.06675/gen_2407_06675.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2407.06675/selftest_report.json)
