+Construction.  H is the matching of q arcs s_r t_r.  Lane r has vertices
+(r,i,x), where i is a layer in {0,...,L} and x is a residue modulo M.  There are
+no cross-lane or nonconsecutive-layer arcs.  Independently sampled units a_ri
+and shifts b_ri define c_ri(x)=a_ri*x+b_ri mod M.  The arcs are exactly
+(r,i,x)->(r,i+1,y) for which c_{r,i+1}(y)-B*c_{r,i}(x) mod M is in
+{0,...,B-1}.  Before any of this is published, the generator samples L base-B
+digits per lane, starts at hidden coordinate zero, and computes the endpoint
+and path.  M=2*B^L+1 prevents wraparound among all source-rooted length-L digit
+strings, so each prescribed pair has exactly one path.  Separate lanes make
+the q paths internally vertex-disjoint by construction.
 
