$$d_{D}(v)<|D_1|+|D_3|+|D_4|+ \frac{a(M)}{15},\ \text{ and } d_{D}^+(w)<\frac{|D_3|-1}{2} + |D_4| + \frac{a(M)}{30}.$$
Together with $|D_1|+|D_2|+|D_3|+|D_4|= n$, it yields that
