For each $i\in [2,s]$, it follows from $(A1)$ that $n_i - 4\leq |G_{i}| = 4\lfloor\frac{n_{i} - 1}{4}\rfloor + 1 \leq n_i $. To ensure that $|G_{i}| = n_{i}$, we remove at most 4 vertices from $S^1_{1}\setminus C$ and add them to $S^{i}_1$. Notice that $\sum_{i \in [q]} n_i \geq n - 100q\rho^2 n$ and some disjoint paths may have been contracted. Thus, to get \(|G_1|=n_1\) (the vertices of the contracted path are also taken into account), we remove some redundant vertices from each set \(S_l^1\), $l\in [4]$ with equality as much as possible. And remove at most $100q\rho^2 n $ vertices in total, while keeping \(|S^1_2| = |S^1_4|\). This results in the number of vertices removed from different sets differing by at most two. Then $|G_1|\geq n_1-650\mu n-100q\rho^2 n\geq 50q\rho n$ as (\ref{para1}).



