/tmp/arxiv-2407.06675-src-XHnjnv/final-Semi-Degree_Condition_for_Arbitrary_H-Linked.tex:212:\begin{proposition}\label{prop1}
/tmp/arxiv-2407.06675-src-XHnjnv/final-Semi-Degree_Condition_for_Arbitrary_H-Linked.tex:213:Let $h$ be an even number, and let $n,q$ be positive integers with $n\geq 3h+7q$. Suppose $H$ is a multi-digraph on $h$ vertices with $q$ arcs that are all directed from $u$ to $v$, where $u,v\in V(H)$. There exists an oriented graph $D$ on $n$ vertices with $\delta^0(D)\geq (3n+3h+3q-13)/8$ such that $D$ is not arbitrary Hamiltonian $H$-linked.
/tmp/arxiv-2407.06675-src-XHnjnv/final-Semi-Degree_Condition_for_Arbitrary_H-Linked.tex:226:From the construction of $D$, we have that
/tmp/arxiv-2407.06675-src-XHnjnv/final-Semi-Degree_Condition_for_Arbitrary_H-Linked.tex:241:We define a bijection \( f: V(H) \to B \) such that \( f(u) = u' \) and \( f(v) = v' \). By the construction of the oriented graph \( D \), for any path from \( u' \) to \( v' \) that is internally disjoint with \( B \), the number of vertices used from \( D_2 \) is at least one more than the number of vertices used from \( D_4 \). Since \( |D_2| = |D_4| + q - 1 \), there are no $q$ internally disjoint $(u',v')$-path. Therefore, \( D \) {is} not arbitrary Hamiltonian \( H \)-linked.
