\begin{lemma}\label{4.5}
\cite{Keevash(2009)} Let $M',n_0$ be positive numbers and let $\varepsilon,d,\eta, \nu,\tau$ be positive constants such that $1/n_0\ll 1/M'\ll \varepsilon \ll d\ll \mu \ll \tau \ll \eta <1$. Let $D$ is an oriented graph on $n\geq n_0$ vertices such that $\delta^0(D)\geq 2\eta n$. Let $R'$ be the reduced digraph of $D$ with parameters $(\varepsilon, d)$ and $|R'|\geq M'$. If $R'$ has a spanning oriented subgraph $R$ with $\delta^0(R)\geq \eta |R|$ such that $R$ is a robust $(\mu, \tau)$-outexpander, then $D$ contains a Hamilton cycle.
